# Every JVM dispatch shape emit-jvm declines, classified. An NTS4009 is
# an override whose representation differs from the method it overrides: the JVM
# refuses it by name, and C and LLVM dispatch it without a check. So each shape is
# either the JVM's alone by construction, or live on C (and then a fixture shows
# it), or refused everywhere once lowering refuses it too, or owned and not yet
# measured. NTS4001 also names conflicting dispatch bodies at one JVM member
# and descriptor, which native tables can distinguish. jvm-verifies.ts fails
# on a dispatch shape not here.
# Rows cover what the runtime and outcomes corpora decline. jvm-verifies --stale lists
# any that neither declines any more, and that row is removed (a decline pinned
# only by a blocker or a crate test belongs to that fixture, not here).
# shape<TAB>verdict<TAB>why -- shapes are normalised (ClosureN, $N$, FnN, TypeN).
ChildWritable._write (Lnts/rt/NtsViewU8;Ljava/lang/String;Lnts/gen/erased/Callable;)V over (Lnts/rt/NtsValue;Ljava/lang/String;Lnts/gen/erased/Callable;)V	refused-everywhere	a narrowed parameter read at an erased argument: was SIGSEGV on C, refused by lowering since b09c3e6f6 -- a-writable-override-narrowing-an-erased-chunk (child_process, cluster)
PerformanceNodeTiming.toJSON ()Lnts/gen/PerformanceNodeTimingJSON; over ()Lnts/gen/PerformanceEntryJSON$Face;	jvm-only	a covariant record repeating the base's fields in its order: a-covariant-record-that-repeats-the-base (reordered would be live: a-covariant-record-with-the-base-fields-reordered)

# Shared assignment checks now count storage refusals too. Each row's native
# behaviour was settled from the layouts (2026-10-11, the JVM lane): a store is
# jvm-only when C's read through the target is the source's own field -- same
# index, same type -- or the target has no field and no slot to read. A row
# stays unmeasured only where no program can reach the store on C.
stateful store TypeN -> TypeN	jvm-only	pre-existing JVM generic-controller assignment refusal in a-controller-stored-by-a-generic-branch; that producer agrees on C
unrelated store URLSearchParamsIteratorImpl -> URLSearchParamsIterator<N>	jvm-only	createIterator's existing store now names the semantic empty target; still held as EventTargetLike with no field or live slot. Same store as the former EventTargetLike/BlobExternalReader keys (47199a39b against 2a4e53739), so C reads nothing through it
unrelated store ReadableStreamAsyncIterator<N> -> AsyncIterableIterator<N>	jvm-only	ReadableStream#values in fs/http/process retains main's iterator store into the same empty EventTargetLike layout, now named by its semantic AsyncIterableIterator identity (08f5ccab1 vs 2a4e53739); no field or live slot can be read through the target. Replaces the former EventTargetLike/Iterable keys
unrelated store FormDataIterator<N> -> IterableIterator<N>	jvm-only	FormData#entries/keys/values in readline/util/fs return into the existing empty EventTargetLike$Face target (no field or live slot to read), matching the URLSearchParamsIterator and ReadableStreamAsyncIterator empty-target rows. The JVM still refuses the store by name; this classifies that JVM decline rather than licensing a store or cast.
stateful store S2 -> CbFace	jvm-only	a-function-field-read-through-an-interface: S2 holds `cb` at index 1 where CbFace has it at 0; main's C, LLVM and RC crashed reading it at CbFace's index, stage B reads it through the accessor family and agrees on C, and the JVM refuses the store by name on both

# One owned stage-C feature. The source plan records each non-prefix transfer
# as FieldView; the JVM refuses that operation, never infers a new store shape.
interface field accessor dispatch	unmeasured	stage C: createCacheStorage RequestContext -> ResponseContext and acquireHTTPParser ParserLease -> HTTPParserLease have no method on main 2a4e53739 (lowering NTS1001 non-prefix transfer), and are newly licensed on native; a-teed-stream-read-back remains stopped on main. Retire this single row when the JVM implements field-family dispatch
